Text=* Schematic File
Text=*
Text=* Syntax:
Text=* .MODEL <model name> [AKO:<reference model name>] <ModelType>
Text=* +([<parameter name>=<value>][LOT[/#][/GAUSS|/UNIFORM|/WCASE]=[<tol>[%]] |[-<low>%,<high>%]][DEV[/#][/GAUSS|/UNIFORM|/WCASE]=[<tol>[%]]...)
Text=* ModelType must be one of OPA,D,NPN,NMOS,NJF,PUL,SIN,TRN,CORE,GASFET,VSWITCH,ISWITCH,CAP,IND,RES,PNP,PMOS,PJF,DOUTPUT,DINPUT,UADC,UDAC,UGATE,UTGATE,UEFF,UGFF,UDLY,UPLD,UROM,URAM,UBGT,UIO,LPNP,NIGBT,I,V
Text=*
Text=*Examples:
Text=* .MODEL 2N2222A NPN(BF=150 IS=1E-14)
Text=* .model M1 NMOS(KP=2.5E-5 VTO=1.345 CGDO=14.67p CGBO=4.566p)
Text=* .MODEL DK D(IS=1E-18)
Text=* .model 2N2222A AKO:2N2222 NPN (BF=55 ISE=10F)
Text=* .Model BJT1 NPN (RE=12 LOT/1/GAUSS=30% DEV/2/UNIFORM=2%)
Text=*
Text=* A .cir file is typically found in the data directory
Text=*
Text=.SUBCKT MCP6001 1 2 3 4 5
Text=*               | | | | |
Text=*               | | | | Output
Text=*               | | | Negative Supply
Text=*               | | Positive Supply
Text=*               | Inverting Input
Text=*               Non-inverting Input
Text=*
Text=********************************************************************************
Text=* Software License Agreement                                                   *
Text=*                                                                              *
Text=* The software supplied herewith by Microchip Technology Incorporated (the     *
Text=* "Company") is intended and supplied to you, the Company's customer, for use  *
Text=* soley and exclusively on Microchip products.                                 *
Text=*                                                                              *
Text=* The software is owned by the Company and/or its supplier, and is protected   *
Text=* under applicable copyright laws. All rights are reserved. Any use in         *
Text=* violation of the foregoing restrictions may subject the user to criminal     *
Text=* sanctions under applicable laws, as well as to civil liability for the       *
Text=* breach of the terms and conditions of this license.                          *
Text=*                                                                              *
Text=* THIS SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED IN AN "AS IS" CONDITION. NO WARRANTIES, WHETHER    *
Text=* EXPRESS, IMPLIED OR STATUTORY, INCLUDING, BUT NOT LIMITED TO, IMPLIED        *
Text=* WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY AND FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE APPLY TO  *
Text=* THIS SOFTWARE. THE COMPANY SHALL NOT, IN ANY CIRCUMSTANCES, BE LIABLE FOR    *
Text=* SPECIAL, INCIDENTAL OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES, FOR ANY REASON WHATSOEVER.     *
Text=********************************************************************************
Text=*
Text=* Macromodel for the MCP6001/2/4 op amp family:
Text=*   MCP6001, MCP6001R, MCP6001U, MCP6002, MCP6004
Text=*
Text=* Revision History:
Text=*   REV A: 21-Jun-02, Created model
Text=*   REV B: 16-Jul-02, Improved output stage
Text=*   REV C: 03-Jan-03, Added MCP6001
Text=*   REV D: 19-Aug-06, Added over temperature, improved output stage, 
Text=*                     fixed overdrive recovery time
Text=*   REV E: 27-Jul-07, Updated output impedance for better model stability w/cap load
Text=*   REV F: 09-Jul-12, Added MCP6001R, MCP6001U
Text=*
Text=* Recommendations:
Text=*   Use PSPICE (other simulators may require translation)
Text=*   For a quick, effective design, use a combination of: data sheet
Text=*     specs, bench testing, and simulations with this macromodel
Text=*   For high impedance circuits, set GMIN=100F in .OPTIONS
Text=*
Text=* Supported:
Text=*   Typical performance for temperature range (-40 to 125) degrees Celsius
Text=*   DC, AC, Transient, and Noise analyses.
Text=*   Most specs, including: offsets, DC PSRR, DC CMRR, input impedance,
Text=*     open loop gain, voltage ranges, supply current, ... , etc.
Text=*   Temperature effects for Ibias, Iquiescent, Iout short circuit 
Text=*   current, Vsat on both rails, Slew Rate vs. Temp and P.S.
Text=*
Text=* Not Supported:
Text=*   Some Variation in specs vs. Power Supply Voltage
Text=*   Monte Carlo (Vos, Ib), Process variation
Text=*   Distortion (detailed non-linear behavior)
Text=*   Behavior outside normal operating region
Text=*
Text=* Input Stage
Text=V10  3 10 -500M
Text=R10 10 11 6.90K 
Text=R11 10 12 6.90K 
Text=C11 11 12 0.2p
Text=C12 1  0 6.00P 
Text=E12 71 14 POLY(4) 20 0 21 0 26 0 27 0   1.00M 20.1 20.1 1 1
Text=G12 1 0 62 0 1m 
Text=M12 11 14 15 15 NMI L=2.00U W=42.0U
Text=M14 12  2 15 15 NMI L=2.00U W=42.0U
Text=G14 2 0 62 0 1m 
Text=C14  2  0 6.00P 
Text=I15 15  4 50.0U
Text=V16 16  4 -300M
Text=GD16 16 1 TABLE {V(16,1)} ((-100,-1p)(0,0)(1m,1n)(2m,1m)(3m,1)) 
Text=V13  3 13 -300M
Text=GD13 2 13 TABLE {V(2,13)} ((-100,-1p)(0,0)(1m,1n)(2m,1m)(3m,1)) 
Text=R70 1 0 20.6T  
Text=R71 2 0 20.6T 
Text=R72 1 2 20T 
Text=I80 1 2 0.5p
Text=*
Text=* Noise, PSRR, and CMRR
Text=I20 21 20 423U
Text=D20 20  0 DN1
Text=D21  0 21 DN1
Text=G26  0 26 POLY(1) 3 4   110U -49U
Text=R26 26  0 1
Text=G27  0 27 POLY(2) 1 0 2 0   -440U 39.7U 39.7U
Text=R27 27  0 1
Text=*
Text=* Open Loop Gain, Slew Rate
Text=G30  0 30 POLY(1) 12 11   0 1
Text=R30 30  0 1K
Text=G31  0 31 POLY(1) 3 4 86 5.25
Text=R31 31  0 1 TC=2.8m
Text=GD31 30 31 TABLE {V(30,31)} ((-11,-1)(-10,-10n)(0,0)(1m,1000))
Text=G32 32  0 POLY(1) 3 4 113.7 3.5
Text=R32 32  0 1 TC=2.65m
Text=GD32 30 32 TABLE {V(30,32)} ((-1m,-1000)(0,0)(10,10n)(11,1))
Text=G33 0 33 30 0 1m
Text=R33 33 0 1k
Text=G34  0 34 33 0 425M
Text=R34  34 0 1K
Text=C34  34 0 74U
Text=G37  0 37 34 0 1m
Text=R37  37 0 1K
Text=C37  37 0 41.6P 
Text=G38  0 38 37 0 1m
Text=R38  39 0 1K
Text=L38  38 39 100U
Text=E38  35 0 38 0 1
Text=G35 33 0 TABLE {V(35,3)} ((-1,-1n)(0,0)(16,1n)(16.1,1))
Text=G36 33 0 TABLE {V(35,4)} ((-16.1,-1)(-16,-1n)(0,0)(1,1n))
Text=*
Text=* Output Stage 
Text=R80 50 0 100MEG
Text=G50 0 50 57 96 2
Text=R58 57  96 0.50
Text=R57 57  0 750
Text=C58  5  0 2.00P
Text=G57  0 57 POLY(3) 3 0 4 0 35 0   0 0.67M 0.67M 1.5M
Text=GD55 55 57 TABLE {V(55,57)} ((-2m,-1)(-1m,-1m)(0,0)(10,1n))
Text=GD56 57 56 TABLE {V(57,56)} ((-2m,-1)(-1m,-1m)(0,0)(10,1n))
Text=E55 55  0 POLY(2) 3 0 51 0 -0.7m 1 -40.0M
Text=E56 56  0 POLY(2) 4 0 52 0 1.2m 1 -37.0M
Text=R51 51 0 1k
Text=R52 52 0 1k
Text=GD51 50 51 TABLE {V(50,51)} ((-10,-1n)(0,0)(1m,1m)(2m,1))
Text=GD52 50 52 TABLE {V(50,52)} ((-2m,-1)(-1m,-1m)(0,0)(10,1n)) 
Text=G53  3  0 POLY(1) 51 0  -49U 1M
Text=G54  0  4 POLY(1) 52 0  -49U -1M
Text=*
Text=* Current Limit 
Text=G99 96 5 99 0 1 
Text=R98 0 98 1 TC=-2.8M,2.63U 
Text=G97 0 98 TABLE { V(96,5) } ((-11.0,-10.0M)(-1.00M,-9.9M)(0,0)(1.00M,9.9M)(11.0,10.0M)) 
Text=E97 99 0 VALUE { V(98)*((V(3)-V(4))*359M + 310M)} 
Text=D98 4 5 DESD 
Text=D99 5 3 DESD 
Text=*
Text=* Temperature / Voltage Sensitive IQuiscent
Text=R61 0 61 100 TC 3.11M 4.51U
Text=G61 3 4 61 0 1
Text=G60 0 61 TABLE {V(3, 4)} 
Text=+ ((0,0)(900M,0.0106U)(1.00,0.20U)(1.3,0.63U)
Text=+ (1.5,0.66U)(1.6,1.06U)(5.5,1.10U))
Text=*
Text=* Temp Sensitive offset voltage 
Text=I73 0 70 DC 1uA 
Text=R74 0 70 1 TC=0
Text=E75 1 71 70 0 1 
Text=*
Text=* Temp Sensistive IBias 
Text=I62 0 62 DC 1uA 
Text=R62 0 62 REXP 58.2u 
Text=* Voltage on R62 used for G12, G14 in input stage
Text=*
Text=* Models
Text=.MODEL NMI NMOS
Text=.MODEL DESD  D   N=1 IS=1.00E-15 
Text=.MODEL DL  D   N=1 IS=1F 
Text=.MODEL DN1 D   IS=1P KF=146E-18 AF=1
Text=.MODEL REXP RES TCE=10.1 
Text=.ENDS MCP6001

